# Intent: Train 5 item B, picture faces on the unit (builds on H02 and H03). The owner's own pictures replace the drawn face. Tools: self.facepic.begin (mode, fps, overlay places), .frame (slot, index, bytes, CRC-32, raw or zlib), .data (a piece at an offset, base64; the offset must equal what the unit has; the last piece checks the CRC), .commit (every frame must be there and a neutral picture; every frame is opened once in the decode task before the pack is promised), .clear and .status. The pack is kept as sent in PSRAM, one frame at a time is decoded by the ROM zlib reader in a low-priority task with a 20 KB PSRAM stack into at most three 153,600 byte PSRAM buffers, and the LVGL task cross-fades between two image layers. Overlay mode hides the face's own eyes and mouth and draws two eyes and a mouth over the picture from the values the fluid face already eases (lid, gaze, drift, mouth weight), so a blink and lip sync come free. Sequence mode plays up to 6 frames of an expression at the pack's rate. A pack that does not fit is refused with a plain sentence in English and Spanish (error and error_es). A mute, vision-off or quiet look, the clock face and a ringing timer always show instead of a picture. Nothing is allocated until a pack is sent; the pack is not kept across a restart, so the host sends it again on connect. A bench build adds self.facepic.bench_force (show one expression, optionally despite a mute) so the pictures can be photographed with self.face.snapshot.
# Placement: unit (decoding, fading and drawing run on the robot; Home down changes nothing once the pack is on the unit)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_decor.cc of this tree for the shape of a face layer; tinfl_decompress_mem_to_mem of the ESP32-S3 ROM miniz (MIT/public domain); lv_image of LVGL 9.5 (MIT)
# Check after a flash: self.facepic.status answers held false and the PSRAM free; push a pack with scripts/fw-pictures.py (bench) or the settings page: the picture shows (not while muted: the mute look shows instead), changes with a short cross-fade when the expression changes, and self.facepic.clear gives the drawn face and the memory back; a pack of too many bytes or frames is refused with the plain sentence; the memory gate holds with a pack held.
